slices.brief:
You build M2's first slice of agentfs, a Rust FUSE filesystem that records every change into git history. The engine is the tree views:
- crates/agentfs-core/src/tree_actor/: the journal, the Shape transition shared by the actor and the builder, a trailing builder writing commits in a hashed layout, the referee and takes;
- crates/agentfs-fuse/src/tree_view.rs: the FUSE view.

Read first:
- docs/trees.md: "What a commit holds", "The journal", "File maps", "The view", "Limits";
- tree_actor/tree.rs: Shape, Names, Shape::apply, Shape::take, Tree::install, Tree::snapshot;
- tree_actor/journal/mod.rs: Change, Entry::Checkpoint, TakeRecord;
- tree_actor/history/format.rs and message.rs;
- tree_actor/recording/mod.rs: the TreeActor file calls, and name() at its end;
- crates/agentfs-core/src/session.rs; crates/agentfs-core/src/tree_git.rs (checkout_entry).

WHAT TO BUILD

1. New module crates/agentfs-core/src/tree_actor/meta.rs: pure values, re-exported from tree_actor (`pub use meta::{Kind, Perm, Attrs, Meta, Times, SetTime}`). Add its row to docs/architecture.md. Signatures:
```rust
use agentfs_contracts::clients::FileOwner;
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[serde(rename_all = "lowercase")]
pub enum Kind { File, Symlink, Dir }
/// mode & 0o7777. JSON: four octal digits ("0644"); anything else fails to parse (Error::Format).
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[serde(into = "String", try_from = "String")]
pub struct Perm(u32);
impl Perm { pub const fn from_mode(mode: u32) -> Self; pub const fn bits(self) -> u32; }
/// What a create or a chmod/chown gives an entry.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Attrs { pub perm: Perm, pub owner: FileOwner }
/// An entry's metadata as history records it; rule M compares it whole.
/// JSON: {"kind":"file","mode":"0644","uid":1000,"gid":1000}
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct Meta { pub kind: Kind, pub mode: Perm, pub uid: u32, pub gid: u32 }
impl Meta {
    /// A Symlink's mode is always 0o777.
    pub const fn new(kind: Kind, attrs: Attrs) -> Self;
    pub const fn attrs(&self) -> Attrs;
    /// 0o120000 Symlink; 0o100755 File with 0o100 set; 0o100644 File otherwise; 0o040000 Dir (never a files/ entry).
    pub const fn git_mode(&self) -> u32;
}
/// Each tree's own; never in history.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub struct Times { pub atime_ns: u64, pub mtime_ns: u64, pub ctime_ns: u64 }
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]
pub enum SetTime { Now, At(u64) }
```

2. Public API, in tree_actor/recording/mod.rs. Mirror every method on SessionGuard (session.rs) without `tree` and `by`, which come from the session.
```rust
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct Node { pub number: Option<u64> /* None: the root directory */, pub meta: Meta, pub times: Times, pub len: u64 /* bytes; a link's target length; 0 for a dir */, pub links: u32 /* 1 named file or link, 0 anonymous, 2 + child dirs for a dir */ }
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct DirEntry { pub name: String, pub number: u64, pub kind: Kind }
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum RenameMode { Replace, NoReplace }
impl TreeActor {
    pub fn node(&self, tree: TreeId, path: &str) -> Result<Node>;  // "" = the root directory
    pub fn node_at(&self, tree: TreeId, number: u64) -> Result<(&str, Node)>; // a named file, link or dir; NotFound otherwise
    pub fn children(&self, tree: TreeId, dir: &str, skip: usize, count: usize) -> Result<Vec<DirEntry>>; // NotFound, NotADirectory; replaces files_from (delete it)
    pub fn mkdir(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, attrs: Attrs, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<u64>;
    pub fn rmdir(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<()>;
    pub fn symlink(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, target: &str, owner: FileOwner, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<u64>;
    pub fn readlink(&self, tree: TreeId, path: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>>;  // Invalid for a non-link
    pub fn set_meta(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, attrs: Attrs, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<()>; // kind kept; "" allowed
    pub fn set_times(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, atime: Option<SetTime>, mtime: Option<SetTime>, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<()>;
    // changed:
    pub fn write_open(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, by: &WriterAt, create: Option<Attrs>) -> Result<u64>;
    pub fn write_open_truncating(&mut self, tree: TreeId, path: &str, by: &WriterAt, create: Option<Attrs>) -> Result<u64>;
    pub fn anonymous_open(&mut self, tree: TreeId, by: &WriterAt, attrs: Attrs) -> Result<u64>;
    pub fn rename(&mut self, tree: TreeId, from: &str, to: &str, mode: RenameMode, by: &WriterAt) -> Result<()>;
}
```
New Error variants, with their errno() mapping:
- NotEmpty: ENOTEMPTY
- NotADirectory: ENOTDIR
- IsADirectory: EISDIR
- Invalid: EINVAL
- NameTooLong: ENAMETOOLONG

Error::Name's text becomes "tree supports git-safe UTF-8 names only".

name() allows '/' (RepoPath rules) and refuses a component over 255 bytes with NameTooLong. A link's target is 1 to 4095 bytes of UTF-8 with no NUL.

3. Journal (journal/mod.rs). Change gains or changes these variants:
```rust
Create { tree: String, path: String, meta: Meta },
Mkdir { tree: String, path: String, meta: Meta },   // dir number = this record's number
Rmdir { tree: String, path: String },
Symlink { tree: String, path: String, meta: Meta }, // object = this record's number; its target's bytes are journal frame bytes, so its map points at them as a write's does (the step's own tail, or one Entry::Bytes record before it as a take's chunks are)
SetMeta { tree: String, path: String, meta: Meta },
SetTimes { tree: String, path: String, atime: Option<SetTime>, mtime: Option<SetTime> }, // builds no commit; build_cost None
```
Rename keeps its shape: for a directory, every entry under it moves.

Other journal changes:
- Entry::AnonymousOpen gains `meta: Meta`.
- TakeRecord gains `pub dirs: Vec<(String, Option<Meta>)>`: each directory the take adds, changes (Some) or removes (None). Shape::take applies them, parents first when adding and children first when removing.
- Entry::Checkpoint gains `locals: BTreeMap<String, TreeLocals>`, where:
```rust
pub(super) struct TreeLocals { pub dirs: BTreeMap<String, (u64, Times)> /* by path; "" the root */, pub files: BTreeMap<u64, Times> /* by identity */ }
```
  Compaction runs only when every step is built, so the actor writes locals from its own Shape. Restore them wherever `objects` is restored.
- Bump FORMAT to "agentfs-trees-11\n".
- Update Record.at_ns's comment: it now also gives the times a tree presents, and still no rule reads it (ledger R2).

4. Shape (tree.rs).
- Add a Dirs map with two keys, by path and by number. Each entry is a DirState { number, meta, times, subdirs: u32 }, and the root is under "".
- Add `meta: BTreeMap<u64, Meta>` and `times: BTreeMap<u64, Times>` by object.
- New signatures:
  - `apply(&mut self, change: &Change, step: EventNumber, at_ns: u64)`
  - `save(&mut self, object, outcome, at_ns)`
  - `add_anonymous(&mut self, object, meta, at_ns)`
- Children are read from the sorted maps by prefix, jumping over each child directory's subtree. There is no second index.
- Rules:
  - parents must exist: NotFound if missing, NotADirectory if not a directory;
  - rmdir needs an empty directory (NotEmpty);
  - unlink of a directory: IsADirectory;
  - rename follows POSIX: dir onto a file is NotADirectory, file onto a dir is IsADirectory, onto a non-empty dir is NotEmpty, onto an empty dir replaces it, into its own subtree is Invalid, onto itself is Ok and changes nothing, and NoReplace onto an existing entry is Exists.
  - A directory rename moves every descendant. Files keep their objects and identities, but they are no longer fresh: each gets a new name version.
- Keys:
  - Key::Name covers directory paths too ("" for the root).
  - A directory step touches the Name of each path it creates, ends or moves, plus each descendant's Name and File.
  - SetMeta of a file touches its File and Name.
- Times:
  - a step sets the ctime of each node it changes;
  - a save sets mtime and ctime;
  - adding, removing or renaming entries sets the parent directories' mtime and ctime;
  - new nodes get the step time;
  - SetTimes sets atime and mtime, with Now meaning the record's at_ns;
  - atime is otherwise the mtime.
- Setgid: in a parent whose mode has 0o2000, a new entry's gid is the parent's, and a new directory keeps 0o2000. This happens in the actor, before the record.
- Shape::take applies TakeRecord.dirs and each file's meta, then checks D1 (every entry's parent is a live directory). A violation is Error::Format.

5. Layout (history/format.rs, feed.rs, builder.rs, message.rs).
- A files/ entry's git mode is meta.git_mode().
- lines/ is `[identity, line map, meta]`.
- Directories go to `dirs/<aa>/<bb>/<enc>`. Here (aa, bb) = fanout(path), and enc replaces '%' with "%25" and then '/' with "%2F".
- The root's record is `dirs/root`, written in the Root commit with Meta { Dir, 0o755, the creating process's euid/egid }. TreeActor::create reads them itself; no signature change.
- Snapshots read dirs/ and meta back.
- ENVELOPE is "Agentfs-Format: envelope-2".
- Subjects: `Mkdir by <writer>`, `Rmdir by <writer>`, `Symlink by <writer>`, `Meta by <writer>` (Cause Direct).
- The builder advances each descendant's NameHistory on a directory rename. Check whether fast-import prunes subtrees that become empty, and make it so.

6. tree_git.rs checkout: a 0o120000 entry is written as a regular file (mode 0o600) holding its target. Never create a symlink in the state area.

7. Interim take rule, in referee/mod.rs and history/take.rs; S3 replaces it.
- `referee::File` gains `pub meta: Meta`, and `referee::Snapshot` gains `pub dirs: BTreeMap<String, Meta>`.
- A file's meta follows the File value the result keeps.
- A take's `dirs` adds every directory of the source snapshot (the fork commit for a landing, the upstream head for a sync) that the target lacks. It removes none and changes no metadata.
- Mark this code with `// Interim until the directory landing rules (MODEL.md R13-R15) are built.`

8. View (tree_view.rs).
- Inodes: 1 is the root; otherwise the node number + 2.
- lookup, readdir and create work in any directory. readdir's '..' carries the parent's inode.
- New ops: mkdir and rmdir.
- create, tmpfile and link take Attrs { perm: Perm::from_mode(mode), owner: FileOwner { uid: req.uid(), gid: req.gid() } }. The kernel has already applied the umask.
- rename works across directories. RENAME_NOREPLACE maps to NoReplace; EXCHANGE and WHITEOUT answer EINVAL.
- getattr comes from node(): kind, perm, nlink, size and times. uid and gid stay the grant's acts_as; S4 switches them to the recorded owner.
- setattr with mode becomes set_meta with the node's recorded owner. uid, gid, atime and mtime stay EOPNOTSUPP until S4.
- The lag gate stands before mkdir, rmdir and set_meta, as before create.
- symlink and readlink are not served yet (S4).

9. Call sites: update every caller of the changed API.
- Tests: give each test file one const Attrs helper.
- crates/agentfs-conformance/src/library.rs (calls).
- crates/agentfs-conformance/src/git_history.rs: parse the lines/ triple.
- ci readers: grep `envelope-1` and `lines/` in ci/ (tree_git_read.py, trees-conformance.py, trees-restart.py, measure-trees.py, tree-git-test-lib.sh, e2e-tree-recording-faults.sh) and update them.
- Grep ci/ for checks of 0600 and 0700 modes and update them.

10. Docs, in the same commit, describing built behaviour only:
- docs/trees.md: commit layout, Terms, the view, Limits. State honestly that owners are still the mount's --owner, and that links and explicit times are not yet served by the view.
- docs/library/core.md: the new API.
- docs/library/filesystem.md.
- docs/architecture.md.
- CHANGELOG.md under Unreleased.

EDGE CASES
- "" is the root directory only for node, children, set_meta and set_times; elsewhere it is Error::Name.
- A take never leaves an entry without its parent.
- Recovery from git plus checkpoint plus replay must give identical numbers and times.
- A directory rename while a file under it is open for writing: the open follows its object, as on Linux.

SIBLINGS: S2 edits crates/agentfs-model in the same checkout and target. A compile error in a file you do not own is its work in progress. Do not edit it; finish your work, rerun, and report it in your result if it persists. Implement only this slice. Do not create, claim or close beads. No timers or sleeps standing in for events. If the frozen interfaces above cannot work, append to .claude/errata.md and STOP.

slices.goal:
The model, crates/agentfs-model and the spec of landing rules, gains the owner-approved rules:
- R13 metadata, with no file times in history;
- R14 directories;
- R15 symbolic links;
- invariant D1.

Each rule is shown by scenarios that read their outcome from git. The ledger, MODEL.md and git-model.md carry the rules as approved. Every existing digest and seed outcome stays byte-identical.

Through the view:
- files show their recorded owners;
- root can chown, the owner can chgrp, and the kernel lets each user do what the modes allow;
- symbolic links can be created, read, renamed and removed;
- `touch -d` and utimensat set times that survive a restart.

`trees mount --owner` (AGENTFS_OWNER) and the grant's acts_as are gone. The tracer's mount root is chowned through the mount, and history records it.

The conformance suite replays the model's directory, metadata and link scenarios on the real library and on real mounts. Each tree's entries, kinds and metadata, and each collision's cause, match the model, and D1 is read from the engine's git history.

The M2 docs close:
- the design page tree-views-beyond-flat-files.md is deleted;
- one-engine.md's M2 row reads built;
- the CHANGELOG lists forks' rules for directories and metadata.

